,'','A','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1004,'What is the name for the remote object proxy that is used by the client?\n','Skeleton','RemoteRef','MarshaledObject','Stub','D','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1005,'grant {\n  keystore \"H:\\.keystore\";\n  grant signedBy \"administrator\" codeBase \"http://www.macs.hw.ac.uk\" {\n    permission java.io.FilePermission \"<<ALL FILES>>\" \"read,write\";\n  }\n};\nThis security policy \n\n\n','defines a keystore called \".keystore\" on the H drive that stores the private key and self-signed certificate for the administrator alias','defines a keystore called \".keystore\" on H drive which holds certificates of trusted subjects','allows the user administrator if his private key and self-signed certificate are held in H:\\.keystore read and write access to all files which can also be accessed via HTTP from www.macs.hw.ac.uk.','Does not allows JAR files signed by administrator whose certificate is signed by a certificate in H:\\.keystore that are fetched by HTTP from www.macs.hw.ac.uk to read and write all local files.  \n','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1006,'RMI uses which payload format?\n','Common Data Representation','serialized Java datatypes','eXtensible Data Representation',' XML','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1007,'RMI uses which method of endpoint addressing?\n','IP address and program number','URL',' IOR','','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1008,'A remote object is passed by?\n','Passed by Copy',' Passed by reference','','','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1009,'An implementation of DGC should ensure\n','Not safety, which implies not collecting too early',' Liveness, which implies eventually collecting','','','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1010,'Due to its inherent decentralized nature, the implementation of DGC is based on reference counting, which poses several issues:\n','It deal properly with circular references\n','It does not deal properly with asynchronous systems','','','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1011,'You need Specify remote   for object being implemented \n','security manager','constructor','interface','implementation','C','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1012,'It is must Define    for remote object to enable its creation \n','security manager','constructor','interface','implementation','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1013,'You have to provide    for remote methods given by remote interface.\n','security manager','constructor','interface','implementation','D','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1014,'Remote objects implement remote interface where \n','remote interface is private',' remote interface extends interface java.rmi.Remote','methods declare java.rmi.Exception in throws clause','objects may not be passed & returned via remote interface \n','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1015,'To write remote object, write class implementing remote interfaces: \n',' specify remote interface(s) being implemented','declaring constructor for remote object','provide implementations for methods invoked locally',' create and install server manager for remote loading \n','A','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1016,'Remote procedure calls typically \n',' support (de)coding of typed data using host/OS neutral routines','Does not permit limited anonymity for talking parties via broadcast RPC',' Does not support naming service to match caller with server procedure \n','','A','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1017,'Java Distributed Object Model supports \n','RMI will not passing remote reference as argument or as result',' casting remote object to any of remote interfaces \n',' using instanceof operator to test remote class','','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1018,'Object serialization supports \n','decoding of objects and datatypes to send as stream of bytes',' construction of object graph at destination','','','B','j2ee',NULL,'Single',0.00,''),(1019,'An object becomes remote by implementing a remote interface, which has the following characteristics: \n\n',' A remote 